+@section band_blur_cuda
+
+Apply configurable blur and luma gradients to a vertical band of an NV12 CUDA
+frame. Pixels outside the band are copied unchanged. The selected band is
+downsampled by two, blurred in two separable passes, and blended back on the
+CUDA device using persistent scratch storage.
+
+It accepts the following options:
+
+@table @option
+@item y_start
+Normalized top coordinate of the band, from 0 to 0.95. The default is 0.70.
+
+@item y_end
+Normalized exclusive lower coordinate of the band, from 0.05 to 1.0. It must
+be greater than @option{y_start}. The default is 1.0.
+
+@item blur_start
+Blurred-image mix at the top of the band, from 0 to 1. The default is 0.
+
+@item blur_end
+Blurred-image mix at the bottom of the band, from 0 to 1. The default is 1.
+
+@item luma_start
+Luma multiplier at the top of the band, from 0 to 2. The default is 1.
+
+@item luma_end
+Luma multiplier at the bottom of the band, from 0 to 2. The default is 0.86.
+
+@item radius
+Blur radius at half resolution, from 1 to 12. The default is 6.
+
+@item gradient
+Interpolation curve. Accepted values are @code{linear} and @code{smoothstep}.
+The default is @code{smoothstep}.
+
+@item gradient_power
+Bias applied after the interpolation curve, from 0.1 to 10. The default is 1.
+@end table
+
+For a top-edge fade, reverse the blur and luma endpoints:
+
+@example
+band_blur_cuda=y_start=0:y_end=.3:blur_start=1:blur_end=0:luma_start=.86:luma_end=1
+@end example
+
 @section colorkey_opencl
 RGB colorspace color keying.
 
